A||||6||Neal||Interesting engine failure||||4||
Z||000000||Neal||09-09-2001||07:31 PM||||Back in april my fiero spun a bearing, or so i thought.  The car has just been sititng since then, with me slowly taking apart the upper end.<P>With the machine shop being almost ready i decided to get my but in gear and yank the bottom end out of the car.<P>A couple of hours later im taking apart the motor, when im backing off the clutch and flywheel bolts there was a knocking every time the crank moved.  Was thinking to myself what the hell kind of spun bearing makes noise now?<P>Finally get the engine striped right down and im doing all the rod bolts but im having the hardest time turning the crank, and then i see it, i never spun a bearing...<P>I broke my crank clean into 2 pieces.  between the 4th cyl and the 3rd main.||||reg||4
Z||000001||maryjane||09-09-2001||07:40 PM||||I've not seen that on a Fiero, but have on large engines (diesels). Usually break at an angle and it still transmits enough torque to allow you to drive, but makes a heck of a noise.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||09-09-2001||07:43 PM||||Cool!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Well, maybe not in the sense that it's a good thing, but it's certainly interesting.||||reg||10
Z||000003||mrfiero||09-09-2001||07:49 PM||||The 2.8 <B><I>does</I></B> have the nickname "crank-breaker"!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||09-09-2001||11:45 PM||||I've heard of just about any engine having this problem...not necessarily more common with with one than any others.  It's kind of a weird deal.<P>I've heard the 2.8 called a LOT of names...but never crank-breaker...?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-09-2001||11:46 PM||||This is a good thing in a way.... probably means the motor need less machine work than you thought.||||reg||1
